{"full":"hf:nandakishorm/vega-ttt","spaceId":"nandakishorm/vega-ttt","name":"Vega 0.8B Typed Decisions","source":"huggingface","description":"Typed decisions with calibrated probabilities, 73k context","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","topics":["gradio","region:us"],"technologies":["Python"],"likes":3,"created":"2026-10-09T14:45:23.000Z","updated":"2026-10-10T19:40:50.000Z","license":null,"runtime":"RUNNING","appUrl":"https://nandakishorm-vega-ttt.hf.space/","demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/nandakishorm/vega-ttt","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T20:59:39.585Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T20:59:39.585Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T20:59:39.585Z","color":"#3c3250","ink":"#e4d4ff","symbol":"⚡","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["One frozen Qwen3.5-0.8B perception stack, read two ways. Every tab shows both, on the same input, so the trade between them is visible rather than asserted.","Measured on the public S1MB evaluator (137 benchmarks, 26,269 decisions) a fitted head lifts Task Avg from 12.75 to 22.56 at +0.063 % latency, and most of that comes from yes/no judgment (boolean 0.131 → 0.333). It is not a free win: where the label space is wide and examples per class are few the head is far worse: −32.5 points on one 268-label benchmark, and it collapses outright on 151-label intent classification, where the engine scores 0.717 and the head 0.000.","So the question is never \"which model\", it is \"does this task have labels\". The Space answers that in front of you: change the input until the two readouts disagree, and the disagreement is the answer."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/nandakishorm/vega-ttt/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"5a8be8087d909031a4ade82d990c508e77cc7fc9dc976d80350967552a96c359","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T20:59:39.666Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T20:59:39.666Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"One frozen Qwen3.5-0.8B percept